# Head-Tracked Desktop Linux Distro — Revised Plan

> **Project name: ViewOS** — *pending trademark verification*.
> This document uses `<DISTRO>` as a placeholder where the name appears in paths.
> Previously drafted as "MyDistro"; "Perceptix" and "Irix" were both investigated and
> **rejected** — see §11 for the reasoning. "ViewOS" is the working name; it has not
> yet been cleared via TESS/EUIPO eSearch (see §11.4).

---

## 0. Executive summary

Build a **publicly released, Debian 13 (Trixie) based, KDE Plasma desktop Linux
distribution** for amd64, with a signature feature: **head-tracked window
perspective** — windows rotate in 3D to face the user's head, using a local webcam,
screen geometry and frustum maths.

Distribution model: Debian's package archive for base packages, plus **one small
signed APT repository of our own** layered on top for our packages and defaults.
Fully free infrastructure — **no paid services, no credit card**.

The project targets **desktop hardware first**. Laptop support is explicitly
deferred (see §3.4 for why this is a deliberate, load-bearing decision).

**Two distinct deliverables with very different risk profiles:**

| Deliverable                | Risk       | Notes                                                       |
|----------------------------|------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
| A working daily-driver ISO | **Medium** | Well-trodden; distros die here on installer + drivers       |
| The face-tilt feature      | **High**   | Unproven UX; real battery/perf cost; needs its own research |

These are deliberately sequenced so that the *boring* deliverable ships first and
validates the infrastructure. See §6.

