## 11. Naming — UNRESOLVED, BLOCKS PHASE 0

### 11.1 Rejected names, with reasons

| Name | Why rejected |
|---|---|
| **Perceptix** | ≥5 active software businesses: Perceptix AI (perceptix.ai), PERCEPTIX AI LIMITED (UK, Jun 2025), Perceptix Technologies LLC (CA, May 2025), perceptix.co.za, perceptix.ch — plus **Perceptix LLC in an active USPTO proceeding**. Critically, several are **AI/vision companies** — the exact class. |
| **Irix / IRIX** | **Silicon Graphics trademark**, USPTO #74484101, **Class 9**, covering *"computer software, namely **operating system software**."* Now "Dead" (not renewed), but SGI's chain ran → Rackable → HP, and SGI's IP is held by Graphics Properties Holdings Inc. — a known patent troll. Also one of the most famous OS names in computing history; permanent brand confusion, down to the iconic wordmark. |
| Sightline | Sightline Systems (commercial monitoring product) |
| Vantage | Lenovo Vantage |
| Cadence | Cadence Design Systems (EDA giant) |
| Sightglass | Existing open-source HTML parser |
| Vantera | Vantara Inc (SF SaaS), Vantera Coffee |
| Vertiq | Nokia EU trademark; Vertiq Software LLC |
| Facetiq | UK company incorporated May 2026 |
| Glance / Glances | Glance (InMobi, 1000+ staff, preinstalled on Samsung/Motorola); GLANCES (Fanatical Labs) |
| Levity | LEVITY AI GmbH — registered Class 42, May 2025 |
| Azimuth | AZIMUTH GRC Inc — registered Class 42 |
| Azimyth | Elysian Masters LLC — Class 9 + 42, filed Mar 2026 |
| Tiltix | POSITAL/FRABA inclinometer hardware |
| Cadensa | Cadensa AI (Oslo); Cadensa Diagnostics |
| Aspect | **Karat Inc — registered EU trademark for "AI software for facial, gesture and speech recognition and analysis"** |
| Sightward | Dead mark, company dissolved 2003 |
| Oblique | Oblique Design LLC; Oblique Inc (IAM vendor) |

### 11.2 The lesson

**The software-naming space, especially around perception/AI/vision, is extremely
crowded.** Every obvious word is taken — and disproportionately by companies in
our exact product category.

**Web search cannot clear a trademark.** A reasonable name found by search can
still collide in a class we did not check.

### 11.3 Chosen working name

**ViewOS** — selected. No existing Linux distribution found by this name. No
obvious trademark conflicts surfaced in web searches, **but web search cannot
clear a trademark.**

### 11.4 Verification procedure (required before public announcement)

1. Search **TESS** — `tmsearch.uspto.gov` (free) for "ViewOS" in Classes 9, 42.
2. Search **EUIPO eSearch** — `euipo.europa.eu/eSearch` (free) for "ViewOS".
3. Check **distro.watch** and LinuxLinks' active-distro list for collisions.
4. Check **domain availability** (`viewos.org`, `viewos.com`, `viewos.io`).
5. If any red flag: pay for a professional clearance search, or pick again.
6. **Then** apply for the Linux Foundation sublicense (§10.1).

> **Note:** The Linux Foundation sublicense is free, perpetual, world-wide, and
> **required** whenever the name contains "Linux" as a brand identifier (e.g.
> "ViewOS Linux"). Apply early — it has lead time.

